<title>CHINA: INDIA'S IFCI SETS US$100 MLN LOAN.</title>
<headline>INDIA'S IFCI SETS US$100 MLN LOAN.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industrial Finance Corporation of India Ltd has launched a US$100 million term loan facility, bankers said.</p>
<p>The seven-year loan has a put option on the fifth anniversary. It pays a margin of 60 basis points over the six-month London Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>With fees, the all-in return for top-tier managers is 65 basis points.</p>
<p>Fuji Bank, Mitsubishi Trust, Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi, Sakura Finance Asia and State Bank of India are arranging for the deal.</p>
<p>General syndication is expected to close by the end of the month.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6960</p>
</text>
